  "articleBody": "Choosing the right contractor for trip hazard repair is key to ensuring a safe and lasting solution. You want someone who really understands the problem, not just someone who can put a band-aid on it. First, consider if the contractor can accurately identify the hazard's source. Is it a surface defect, a structural settlement issue, or a code safety threshold problem? They should be able to distinguish between these. Next, ask about the repair method they offer. Will it be a permanent fix, or just a temporary one? You definitely want a solution that addresses the root cause, not just the visible symptom. It's also vital that they can measure and document the defect, which shows they're taking a precise approach. Make sure they can handle your specific flooring material—whether it's carpet, tile, vinyl, or concrete. A good contractor will discuss how they'll address recurring contributors like settlement or uneven transitions to prevent the hazard from coming back. When the hazard is a structural condition, or if the repair affects a main circulation route, hiring a qualified professional who offers precise measurement and durable correction, like us at HH Remodeling LLC, is incredibly important. Give us a call at 303-505-0866 to discuss your needs.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
